<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#incense">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Incense</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Incense is aromatic resin or plant material burned for its fragrance, especially in religious rituals. Frankincense and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myrrh">myrrh</a> from north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> were highly valued in the ancient world. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> took part in trade in incense and other luxury goods of the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/incense.jpg" alt="Incense" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: nakimusi · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Incense_burner_at_Yakuo-in.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
